{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat task.md output_contract.md 00_intake_brief.md 01_selection_rules.md 04_storage_update_2026-05-06.md 07_budget_and_costs.md 08_site_notes_roundup.md 09_future_wave_requests.md 10_archived_policy_excerpt.md 11_optional_addons.md && cat 02_site_roster.csv 03_storage_audit_2026-04-18.csv 05_coordinator_availability.csv 06_transport_quotes.csv'","aggregated_output":"# Clinic Rollout Plan\n\nYou are helping finalize the first-wave clinic rollout for a medication cooler deployment.\n\nRead all files in this folder. Choose exactly three first-wave clinics using the current selection rules, clinic files, storage evidence, coordinator availability, transport quotes, and budget notes. If files conflict, use the source reliability rules in `01_selection_rules.md`.\n\nCreate the deliverables listed in `output_contract.md` inside an `answer/` folder in this task folder. The goal is to leave behind useful rollout artifacts that another operations coordinator could review.\n\nYour work must make the source-resolution step, clinic-screening step, and final launch recommendation visible as separate checkpoints.\n# Deliverable Contract\n\nCreate an `answer/` folder in this task folder, then create these three files inside it. The format may be Markdown tables or concise labeled sections, but the paths, filenames, and required facts must be present.\n\n## `answer/source_resolution.md`\n\nRecord which sources control the first-wave clinic decision when files conflict or distract from the current rollout.\n\nRequired facts:\n\n- The source reliability rule from `01_selection_rules.md`.\n- A note that `04_storage_update_2026-05-06.md` is newer than `02_site_roster.csv` and `03_storage_audit_2026-04-18.csv` for storage-status conflicts.\n- The effective storage status and source used for every clinic in `02_site_roster.csv`.\n- A note that archived policy excerpts, future-wave requests, and optional add-ons do not override the current first-wave selection rules.\n\n## `answer/clinic_screen.md`\n\nScreen every clinic against the first-wave requirements.\n\nRequired facts:\n\n- One row or entry for every clinic in `02_site_roster.csv`.\n- For each clinic: effective storage status, coordinator full-window availability, transport delivery date, total rollout cost if otherwise eligible, eligible `yes` or `no`, and the blocking reason when ineligible.\n- The current first-wave budget.\n- The selected-clinic total cost calculation.\n\n## `answer/launch_recommendation.md`\n\nWrite the final recommendation for the rollout coordinator.\n\nRequired facts:\n\n- The three selected clinics.\n- Total rollout cost and remaining budget.\n- The anchor clinic and donor continuity code from the intake brief.\n- The carrier and delivery date for each selected clinic.\n- Short rejected-clinic summary.\n\nRules:\n\n- Use local files only.\n- Do not put the required deliverables in the task root; put them under `answer/`.\n- Use dollar amounts rounded to whole dollars unless a source provides cents.\n- Extra scratch files are allowed, but scoring is based on the three named deliverables under `answer/`.\n# Intake Brief\n\nDate: 2026-05-09\n\nThe first-wave medication cooler rollout needs a short recommendation packet for the operations coordinator. The packet should select exactly three North-region clinics that can receive cooler kits before the June launch window.\n\nKeep this continuity fact with the final recommendation: Maple Junction Clinic is the donor continuity anchor if it remains eligible, and its donor continuity code is `MJ-14`. The code was printed on already-approved training inserts and is not repeated in the later operations files.\n\nThe launch window is 2026-06-10 through 2026-06-14. All selected clinics need coordinator coverage for the full window and delivery no later than 2026-06-07.\n\nDo not include a separate narrative for future-wave clinic requests unless they change current first-wave eligibility.\n# Selection Rules\n\nEffective date: 2026-05-08\n\n## Source Reliability\n\n- When two files disagree about the same clinic eligibility field, use the newest dated source for that field.\n- Files titled or labeled as archived, future wave, or optional add-ons are planning context only. They do not override current first-wave selection rules.\n- The clinic roster gives baseline information, but newer storage updates control storage status where they conflict.\n\n## First-Wave Requirements\n\nSelect exactly three clinics. A selected clinic must satisfy all of these requirements:\n\n- Region is `North`.\n- Clinic status is `open` for the 2026-06-10 to 2026-06-14 launch window.\n- Effective storage status is accepted for first-wave use. Accepted statuses are `certified` and `certified after mitigation complete`. Not accepted: `expired`, `suspended`, `conditional pass pending`, or any status awaiting repair.\n- The named coordinator is available for the full launch window.\n- Transport delivery is no later than 2026-06-07.\n- Selected-clinic total rollout cost stays within the first-wave budget in `07_budget_and_costs.md`.\n\n## Selection Preference\n\n- Include the donor continuity anchor if it is eligible.\n- If more than three clinics are eligible, choose the anchor plus the lowest-cost eligible clinics.\n- If fewer than three clinics are eligible, choose only eligible clinics and flag the gap instead of relaxing hard requirements.\n# Storage Update\n\nDate: 2026-05-06\n\nUse this update for storage status where it conflicts with the roster or the 2026-04-18 audit.\n\n- `N-102` Riverbend Health: temperature logger installation was verified on 2026-05-05. Treat as `certified after mitigation complete` for first-wave use.\n- `N-104` Lakeside Family Care: cooler certification is `suspended` after a compressor fault found on 2026-05-04. Earliest retest is after 2026-06-15.\n- `N-106` Hillcrest Annex: recertification was completed on 2026-05-05. Treat as `certified` for first-wave use.\n- `N-107` Old Mill Clinic: door seal repair was delayed. Status remains `conditional pass pending` and is not accepted for first-wave use.\n\nNo newer storage changes are available for the other clinics.\n# Budget And Cost Notes\n\nDate: 2026-05-08\n\nThe first-wave budget is `$20,000` for setup costs plus required transport costs.\n\nUse `setup_cost` from `02_site_roster.csv` and `transport_cost` from `06_transport_quotes.csv` to calculate each clinic's rollout cost. Optional add-ons, future-wave requests, and staff celebration supplies are not part of the first-wave budget.\n\nThe budget owner wants the recommendation to show the selected-clinic total and the remaining budget.\n# Site Notes Roundup\n\nDate: 2026-05-07\n\nThese notes may help explain choices, but they do not override the selection rules.\n\n- Maple Junction Clinic has already hosted one cooler-handling practice session with Iris Patel.\n- Riverbend Health asked for a short remote setup call because the temperature logger is new.\n- Pine Ridge Outreach has strong patient demand, but Lena Torres is unavailable on 2026-06-12.\n- Lakeside Family Care expects its compressor repair in mid-June, after the first-wave launch window.\n- Cedar Works Clinic is popular with outreach staff, but the building is unavailable during maintenance closure.\n- Hillcrest Annex is small but has clear receiving instructions and Mara Ives confirmed launch-week coverage.\n- Old Mill Clinic is interested in a later rollout after the door seal repair is complete.\n# Future-Wave Requests\n\nDate: 2026-05-03\n\nThe following requests are for a later wave and should not be treated as first-wave requirements.\n\n- South Gate Clinic asked to join the next South-region wave because CityCourier has a low transport quote.\n- Lakeside Family Care asked to be reconsidered after the compressor retest.\n- Old Mill Clinic asked for a replacement door seal kit before a later wave.\n- Cedar Works Clinic asked for advance notice once maintenance dates are confirmed.\n\nThese requests are useful planning context only.\n# Archived Policy Excerpt\n\nArchived date: 2026-03-12\n\nThis archived excerpt is kept for historical context. It does not control the current first-wave rollout.\n\nOld guidance selected two clinics per wave and prioritized the lowest total transport cost. The current first-wave rules replaced this guidance after the May operating review.\n# Optional Add-Ons\n\nDate: 2026-05-02\n\nThese add-ons are optional and are not part of first-wave eligibility or the budget calculation unless a later approval says otherwise.\n\n| Add-on | Cost | Notes |\n| --- | ---: | --- |\n| Extra laminated quick cards | 450 | Nice to have for larger sites. |\n| On-site celebration snacks | 300 | Requested by two coordinators, not required for launch. |\n| Spare thermometer bundle | 525 | Useful backup inventory, not tied to site eligibility. |\n| Branded tote bags | 375 | Outreach request for a later campaign. |\nclinic_id,clinic_name,region,clinic_status,baseline_storage_status,setup_cost,coordinator\nN-101,Maple Junction Clinic,North,open,certified,6200,Iris Patel\nN-102,Riverbend Health,North,open,conditional pass pending,5500,Omar Singh\nN-103,Pine Ridge Outreach,North,open,certified,4800,Lena Torres\nN-104,Lakeside Family Care,North,open,certified,4700,Noah Brooks\nN-105,Cedar Works Clinic,North,closed maintenance,certified,3600,Sima Cho\nN-106,Hillcrest Annex,North,open,expired,4100,Mara Ives\nN-107,Old Mill Clinic,North,open,conditional pass pending,3500,Tao Nguyen\nS-201,South Gate Clinic,South,open,certified,3900,Dee Alvarez\nclinic_id,audit_date,audit_storage_status,audit_note\nN-101,2026-04-18,certified,Passed cooler inspection with no mitigation items.\nN-102,2026-04-18,conditional pass pending,Temperature logger installation was still pending.\nN-103,2026-04-18,certified,Passed cooler inspection with no mitigation items.\nN-104,2026-04-18,certified,Passed cooler inspection with no mitigation items.\nN-105,2026-04-18,certified,Passed cooler inspection before maintenance closure notice.\nN-106,2026-04-18,expired,Certification expired before recertification visit.\nN-107,2026-04-18,conditional pass pending,Door seal repair was still pending.\nS-201,2026-04-18,certified,Passed cooler inspection with no mitigation items.\nclinic_id,coordinator,available_full_launch_window,blackout_dates,notes\nN-101,Iris Patel,yes,,Confirmed for 2026-06-10 through 2026-06-14.\nN-102,Omar Singh,yes,,Confirmed for 2026-06-10 through 2026-06-14.\nN-103,Lena Torres,no,2026-06-12,Required training blackout on 2026-06-12.\nN-104,Noah Brooks,yes,,Confirmed for 2026-06-10 through 2026-06-14.\nN-105,Sima Cho,yes,,Available but clinic is closed for maintenance.\nN-106,Mara Ives,yes,,Confirmed for 2026-06-10 through 2026-06-14.\nN-107,Tao Nguyen,yes,,Confirmed for 2026-06-10 through 2026-06-14.\nS-201,Dee Alvarez,yes,,Confirmed for 2026-06-10 through 2026-06-14.\nclinic_id,carrier,quote_date,delivery_by,transport_cost,notes\nN-101,SwiftRoute,2026-05-01,2026-06-06,1200,Direct cold-chain route available.\nN-102,NorthLine,2026-05-01,2026-06-07,950,Delivery lands on the latest acceptable date.\nN-103,SwiftRoute,2026-05-01,2026-06-05,700,Direct cold-chain route available.\nN-104,SwiftRoute,2026-05-01,2026-06-06,650,Direct cold-chain route available.\nN-105,NorthLine,2026-05-01,2026-06-08,500,Delivery misses first-wave cutoff.\nN-106,Valley Freight,2026-05-02,2026-06-07,850,Delivery lands on the latest acceptable date.\nN-107,SwiftRoute,2026-05-01,2026-06-05,600,Direct cold-chain route available.\nS-201,CityCourier,2026-05-01,2026-06-05,500,South-region route only.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
